From: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@1bit.gg>
Subject: [PATCH] ec_su_axb35: attach only on an AXB35 board

The driver talks to the board's embedded controller at fixed EC registers
(0x21/0x23/0x25 for the fan modes, 0x35-0x38 for the tachometers). Those are
the AXB35-02's registers; on any other machine the same addresses belong to a
different chip, so loading it there writes blind into a stranger's EC.

The dkms package is installed wherever the package set is, so ask the DMI
board name first and touch nothing when it is not an AXB35. Returning 0
rather than -ENODEV is deliberate: the package drops a modules-load.d entry,
and a loaded-but-idle module is a quieter outcome on a non-AXB35 box than a
failed unit at every boot.

Signed-off-by: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@1bit.gg>
---
--- a/src/ec_su_axb35.c
+++ b/src/ec_su_axb35.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/fs.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
@@ -529,9 +530,21 @@
 
 static int __init ec_su_axb35_init(void)
 {
+    const char *board = dmi_get_system_info(DMI_BOARD_NAME);
     int i;
     int ret;
 
+    /*
+     * The EC registers this driver owns are the AXB35-02's; on any other
+     * board they belong to a different controller. Do not write to them:
+     * report the board found and leave the module loaded and idle.
+     */
+    if (!board || !strstr(board, "AXB35")) {
+        pr_info("ec_su_axb35: board is %s, not an AXB35: not attaching\n",
+                board ? board : "(no DMI board name)");
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     ret = alloc_chrdev_region(&ec_su_axb35_dev, 0, ARRAY_SIZE(ec_fans) + 2,
                               "ec_su_axb35");
     if (ret < 0) {
